From edb3883b78ec90960343315031524b728823db0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sfxnz <sfxnz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:24:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] inkling2: deduplicate loop AR, batch pass messages, tile
 small-M gates, use mix_rows

Commit 1 (Lever 5, 100% lossless, zero extra VRAM):
- Deduplicate 40 sliding tf_ink2_loop_ar launches per round on core passes 2 and 3
  by running attention controller roles in reverse order (2, 1, 0) against shared AR output
  (inspired by MiaAI-Lab commit 9e3cf20b patch 0005-mini-speed.patch).
- Batch tf_ink2_loop_messages once per core pass (12 layers in 1 launch instead of 24)
  when rows * core_layers <= prompt_rows, gated by TF_INKLING2_PASS_MESSAGES (default 1).
- Default ops.mix to tf_ink2_mix_rows (with TF_INKLING2_MIX_NARROW=1 opt-in, adapted from
  MiaAI-Lab 0005-mini-speed.patch) and add a 1-pass 5-register FP32 RMSNorm fast path in
  tf_ink2_mix_rows for the 96 query==0 post-gate calls per round.
- Add bit-exact 8-row tiled tf_ink2_loop_gate_down_tiled for 2 <= rows <= 128 (leaving
  rows == 1 on gateDown and rows > 128 on existing 2-row gateDownPrepared so 4K/32K prefill
  is untouched) and lower gateUpTiled threshold from rows >= 8 to rows >= 2.
- Vectorize tf_ink2_rel_table with uint4 16-byte loads/stores at 128 threads/block
  (adapted from MiaAI-Lab 0005-mini-speed.patch).
